# Byte-exact checkout, everywhere, deliberately.
#
# This repository records checksums of its own data: MD5 of the pinned source
# database in data/raw/PROVENANCE.md, and SHA-256 of the three release tables
# in reports/phase4/release_summary.json. scripts/p4_05_verify.py recomputes
# the SHA-256 values and fails if they disagree.
#
# Git's line-ending conversion is per-platform, so with conversion enabled a
# reviewer cloning on Linux and a reviewer cloning on Windows get different
# bytes for the same commit, and at most one of them can match a recorded
# checksum. Disabling it means every clone is byte-identical and the repository
# verifies against itself anywhere.
#
# The cost is that text files keep whatever line endings they were committed
# with. For a published analysis that is the right trade.
* -text
